{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You were brought in because your blood sugar was very high—over 400. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, at my radiation appointment, they checked my blood sugar and it was really high. I’ve been taking my insulin like always—Lantus at night and Humalog when needed—but it’s not helping since I started dexamethasone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Dexamethasone, the steroid you started for your back pain from the spinal fracture, can raise blood sugar a lot, especially in people with diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so that’s why? I was worried I was doing something wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. You’re doing everything right. The steroid changes how your body handles sugar. We’ll adjust your insulin while you’re on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. I also almost fell at the clinic. My left knee just gave out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I saw that. Any pain or weakness in the knee?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s not painful. But I’ve had these numb feet for years from diabetes. I think I just lost balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your peripheral neuropathy could be contributing. We’ll keep an eye on your mobility. No signs of injury, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been falling a few times at home too. Nothing serious, but it’s scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your recent hospitalization and long recovery, you’re probably deconditioned. That means your strength and balance aren’t where they used to be."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds right. I haven’t been walking much since last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get physical therapy involved to help you rebuild strength and prevent falls."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would be great. And my kidneys—my last creatinine was up, wasn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine was 1.6, up from 1.2. That likely means mild kidney injury from dehydration. We’re giving you IV fluids to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been drinking much—my mouth’s been dry with the high sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. High glucose pulls fluid from your body. We’ll recheck your kidney function tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my myeloma? I restarted Revlimid recently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your Revlimid and other myeloma meds. Your oncologist is aware, and you’ll keep up with radiation for the spinal fracture as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-10-03 17:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want to fall behind on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning, Mr. ___. Your blood sugar this morning is 240—much better than 448. And your creatinine dropped to 1.3, so your kidneys are improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. Is the insulin working better now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and the endocrine team recommended increasing your Lantus from 30 to 35 units on days you take dexamethasone, and adding 4 units to each Humalog dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. Will I need to see the endocrinologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they recommend follow-up with your endocrinologist to monitor this long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my feet—they’re still numb. Is that getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your exam still shows decreased sensation in your feet, worse on the left. That’s consistent with diabetic neuropathy. You’re on gabapentin, amitriptyline, and duloxetine—that’s a strong regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It helps a little, but the tingling never goes away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can discuss adjustments with your neurologist, but managing blood sugar is key to preventing further nerve damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. Oh, and I had a little scare yesterday—I tripped over my IV pole when the door closed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nurse documented a mechanical fall—no injury, thankfully. It’s another reason we’re getting PT involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit unsteady, especially with distractions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2173-10-04 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. PT will work on balance and safe walking. We’ll also make sure you have your cane and use it consistently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar this morning is 194—well-controlled. Creatinine is now 1.2, back to baseline. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. We’ll send you home with physical therapy to help with strength and prevent falls."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my insulin changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll increase Lantus to 35 units and add 4 units to each Humalog dose on dexamethasone days. Follow up with your endocrinologist in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my oncologist? For the myeloma and radiation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, follow up with Dr. ___ for your myeloma. Continue Revlimid and finish your radiation series as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the falls? Should I see someone about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Please follow up with your primary care doctor. They can assess for other causes and coordinate with PT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on lamivudine for hepatitis B—still okay to continue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your viral load is undetectable. Keep taking it as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your medications remain unchanged, including your pain, blood pressure, and depression meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2173-10-05 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-10-03 17:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-10-05 18:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with severe hyperglycemia in the setting of dexamethasone therapy for a pathologic spinal fracture related to multiple myeloma. His blood glucose reached the 400s despite adherence to his home insulin regimen. He also presented with acute kidney injury, likely due to volume depletion, and a history of recurrent falls attributed to diabetic neuropathy and deconditioning from a prior prolonged hospitalization. During admission, his blood sugar improved with insulin adjustment and his renal function normalized with IV fluids. An endocrinology recommendation was implemented to increase his basal and bolus insulin on steroid days. He remained stable, with no infectious complications, and was discharged home with physical therapy for fall prevention and plans for outpatient follow-up with his endocrinologist, oncologist, and primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Multiple myeloma, without mention of having achieved remission",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without mention of hepatic coma without mention of hepatitis delta",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Sickle-cell trait",
      "Unspecified sleep apnea",
      "Alcohol abuse, in remission",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "History of fall",
      "Peripheral stem cells replaced by transplant",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of prostate"
    ]
  }
}
